student_response:
I’m sorry—I made a mistake.  

When you divide a fraction by a whole number you keep the numerator the same and multiply the denominator by that number (or, equivalently, multiply by the reciprocal).  

So  

\[
\frac{3}{11}\div 3 \;=\; \frac{3}{11}\times\frac{1}{3}
\;=\; \frac{3\cdot 1}{11\cdot 3}
\;=\; \frac{3}{33}
\;=\; \frac{1}{11}.
\]

Therefore the correct choice is **D. \(\displaystyle \frac{1}{11}\)**. Thank you for pointing out the error!

